-The NeRF Training Loop is the iterative optimization procedure that minimizes the photometric error between rendered images and ground-truth observations by updating the parameters of a neural radiance field [S6, S16, unofficial]. It solves the inverse rendering problem by differentiating the volume rendering equation with respect to the scene representation, enabling gradient-based learning of geometry and appearance [44-radiance-field-optimization.md]. It sets itself apart from [NeRF Evaluation and Metric Calculation](3079-nerf-evaluation-and-metric-calculation.md) by using stochastic ray sampling and adaptive integration strategies to facilitate gradient propagation, rather than deterministic rendering for metric assessment [S2][S3, S5, S10, unofficial].
